When using the proxy-backend plugin, if you want to proxy connections to gitlab, you may want to add an authorization typ header leveraging a Gitlab Private Access Token.  When doing that you add a header of `PRIVATE-TOKEN: <gitlab personal access token>` for the authentication/authorization.  In the plugin's [config.d.ts](https://github.com/backstage/backstage/blob/c667c2bf906d9c0ea58d2066b5e9c2bd64f95c76/plugins/proxy-backend/config.d.ts#L45) it allows for `/** @visibility secret */` for various types of header like `Authorization`, but not for `PRIVATE-TOKEN` so you can see the token value in the UI /devtools/config page.

